{"lines":[{"y":0.038245858311480085,"w":0.084409287770589203,"c":1,"x":0.8190407542027075,"h":0.017393608925127202,"t":"Reading"},{"h":0.015988371899566256,"y":0.087209302417118884,"t":"READING PASSAGE 3","c":1,"x":0.069902914746425612,"w":0.30679611206054686},{"w":0.82158935546875,"c":1,"x":0.069779461963896575,"t":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 27-40, which are based on Reading","y":0.12463873519250934,"h":0.023343879485798746},{"x":0.067961165671369769,"w":0.16893203735351564,"t":"Passage 3 below.","y":0.14534883729461057,"h":0.016021879439784725,"c":1},{"c":1,"h":0.02622708828649789,"y":0.19034267931203508,"w":0.59999999999999998,"t":"Conquering Earth's space junk problem","x":0.18446601921311698},{"t":"C","y":0.82703488352900845,"w":0.017475727399190275,"c":1,"h":0.01308139551465759,"x":0.064077670200081246},{"y":0.23389087699869426,"w":0.76710647583007807,"t":"Satellites, rocket shards and collision debris are creating major traffic risks in orbit","h":0.019572434469918187,"c":1,"x":0.10090613421905743},{"w":0.6368932088216146,"h":0.016199376947040545,"y":0.25420560751482768,"x":0.16504854111247388,"c":1,"t":"around the planet. Researchers are working to reduce these threats"},{"h":0.019003115264797588,"c":1,"t":"Last year, commercial companies, military and civil departments and amateurs","x":0.11262136054857062,"w":0.73786407470703119,"y":0.28193146423952631},{"w":0.7147594197591145,"c":1,"t":"sent more than 400 satellites into orbit, over four times the yearly average in","x":0.11252262170002666,"h":0.020567800694165417,"y":0.29938626069878782},{"y":0.31870123400771144,"x":0.11061248782466028,"t":"the previous decade. Numbers could rise even more sharply if leading space","w":0.72246714274088542,"h":0.019029926288165022,"c":1},{"x":0.1125552768712698,"w":0.71858083089192715,"y":0.33690119982800304,"c":1,"h":0.020523350558176889,"t":"companies follow through on plans to deploy hundreds to thousands of large"},{"t":"constellations of satellites to space in the next few years.","x":0.11247324789708738,"h":0.020465686833747054,"y":0.35498939981739697,"w":0.53628631591796883,"c":1},{"h":0.019859886763623269,"y":0.38514800485042877,"c":1,"x":0.11255393768180814,"w":0.7787659708658855,"t":"All that traffic can lead to disaster. Ten years ago, a US commercial Iridium satellite"},{"c":1,"t":"smashed into an inactive Russian communications satellite called Cosmos-2251,","x":0.11248011020178182,"w":0.76346852620442707,"h":0.024798417611285539,"y":0.39971023783203385},{"c":1,"w":0.71650487263997398,"h":0.017533326074713251,"t":"creating thousands of new pieces of space shrapnel that now threaten other","x":0.11262134985234316,"y":0.4229651161467205},{"h":0.020745012990410761,"c":1,"t":"satellites in low Earth orbit - the zone stretching up to 2,000 kilometres in altitude.","y":0.44006359940486406,"w":0.77110341389973958,"x":0.112519510051726},{"w":0.7457640584309897,"t":"Altogether, there are roughly 20,000 human-made objects in orbit, from working","x":0.11255738346421586,"y":0.45950055401016188,"c":1,"h":0.020177022393247479},{"h":0.020638227611315951,"c":1,"t":"satellites to small rocket pieces. And satellite operators can't steer away from every","y":0.47794368600002857,"x":0.11254700442612356,"w":0.78074030558268237},{"h":0.017546004892509681,"w":0.76504852294921877,"c":1,"t":"potential crash, because each move consumes time and fuel that could otherwise","y":0.49844236730771918,"x":0.11262136945571835},{"w":0.35533978780110675,"x":0.11262136991012625,"y":0.51588785033217666,"h":0.017542381524296879,"c":1,"t":"be used for the spacecraft's main job."},{"c":1,"y":0.54500478601369839,"x":0.10091584479125554,"w":0.76903620402018236,"t":"Concern about space junk goes back to the beginning of the satellite era, but the","h":0.019121114784311999},{"y":0.56183708421455991,"w":0.73412353515625006,"c":1,"t":"number of objects in orbit is rising so rapidly that researchers are investigating","x":0.11061952901572075,"h":0.021159631366670317},{"c":1,"t":"new ways of attacking the problem. Several teams are trying to improve methods","y":0.58141921686479359,"h":0.021154252762363712,"w":0.76134816487630208,"x":0.11059023235067428},{"y":0.60116812139553311,"t":"for assessing what is in orbit, so that satellite operators can work more efficiently","h":0.0195083897433177,"x":0.1086698775677606,"w":0.759368896484375,"c":1},{"t":"in ever-more-crowded space. Some researchers are now starting to compile a","x":0.10864309565138257,"y":0.61899032370824625,"h":0.019603129116545603,"w":0.73417800903320318,"c":1},{"t":"massive data set that includes the best possible information on where everything is","y":0.63796626178035376,"c":1,"x":0.11257335108384685,"w":0.77874186197916673,"h":0.019181223598967456},{"c":1,"x":0.10867241228770913,"t":"in orbit. Others are developing taxonomies of space debris - working on measuring","y":0.65629948044137698,"w":0.78266977945963556,"h":0.019943396547501657},{"x":0.11062900681386575,"h":0.019934902012905265,"c":1,"y":0.67567061346861268,"t":"properties such as the shape and size of an object, so that satellite operators know","w":0.7787530008951824},{"y":0.69470405003363767,"w":0.47572814941406255,"h":0.017505252398434368,"c":1,"x":0.11067961450362579,"t":"how much to worry about what's coming their way."},{"h":0.017595812836168734,"c":1,"t":"The alternative, many say, is unthinkable. Just a few uncontrolled space crashes","x":0.1106796077896875,"y":0.72383720918812977,"w":0.75533981323242183},{"w":0.78275843302408854,"x":0.11057187980254297,"c":1,"y":0.73999894328514193,"t":"could generate enough debris to set off a runaway cascade of fragments, rendering","h":0.022120920817057299},{"t":"near-Earth space unusable. 'If we go on like this, we will reach a point of no return,'","w":0.7825242614746093,"y":0.76012461034064371,"x":0.11067961674543246,"c":1,"h":0.019003115264797588},{"y":0.77906976732859667,"x":0.11067961920536599,"w":0.74563105265299479,"t":"says Carolin Frueh, an astrodynamical researcher at Purdue University in West","h":0.017503441308517664,"c":1},{"t":"Lafayette, Indiana.","h":0.01904114993561834,"w":0.17864077250162763,"x":0.11067961363535962,"y":0.79781931488800428,"c":1},{"t":"Even as our ability to monitor space objects increases, so too does the total","x":0.11061884760878002,"h":0.019397552585304734,"y":0.82700379690739312,"w":0.71079340616861975,"c":1},{"h":0.019031188346886552,"w":0.78058252970377606,"c":1,"x":0.11067960884877304,"t":"number of items in orbit. That means companies, governments and other players in","y":0.84579439276940338},{"t":"space are collaborating in new ways to avoid a shared threat. International groups","y":0.86414734272684035,"x":0.11060650165560285,"w":0.77100733439127622,"h":0.019767293603249358,"c":1},{"t":"such as the Inter-Agency Space Debris Coordination Committee have developed","x":0.11067962360855338,"y":0.88372093011848052,"w":0.75922327677408852,"h":0.017525175575898055,"c":1},{"h":0.017565928069973369,"w":0.71650487263997398,"c":1,"y":0.90249221157053017,"x":0.11067960234218181,"t":"guidelines on space sustainability. Those include inactivating satellites at the"},{"x":0.11060764602245995,"h":0.020629300506686876,"w":0.75354248046875005,"y":0.91986740090162167,"c":1,"t":"end of their useful life by venting pressurised materials or leftover fuel that might"},{"x":0.86990291354066529,"c":1,"h":0.014534883112922281,"y":0.95494186058743424,"w":0.029126211802164681,"t":"25"}],"h":3209,"w":2400}